WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:39.520
The 47 Ronin - Japan’s Greatest Tale of
Vengeance

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.760
This tremendous tale of samurai loyalty and
honor goes by several names.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:50.040
It is usually referred to as the Akō jiken
in Japan, translated as the Akō incident,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.340
or sometimes the Akō vendetta.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:56.980
It has been featured so prominently in Japanese
literature and kabuki theater that it spawned

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:03.870
its own genre - Chūshingura, or The Treasure
of Loyal Retainers, that only includes fictional

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.670
stories based on this historical event.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.470
In the West, we know it as The 47 Ronin - the
story of 47 early 18th-century samurai who

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:17.860
lose their master and embark on an ambitious
journey to avenge the unjust death of their

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:18.860
lord.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:23.150
The tale first made its way to our parts over
a hundred years after it took place courtesy

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:28.260
of Isaac Titsingh, a Dutch merchant and scholar
who did business with the Tokugawa shogunate

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.290
of Japan on behalf of the Dutch East India
Company.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:36.520
The event was later popularized by British
writer and former diplomat A.B. Mitford who

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.470
featured it prominently in his anthology book
Tales of Old Japan.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.960
This has become the definitive version of
the story in the West and the one we will

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.330
be mostly relying on today.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.670
Modern scholars opine that, while Mitford
did do plenty of research for his book and

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:57.159
presents a lot of details and descriptions,
he also had a habit of overdramatizing some

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:01.510
of the more climactic parts to make for a
more exciting story.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:08.690
Even so, today we bring you, as best we know
it, the tale of the 47 ronin.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.810
The Death of Asano Naganori

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.730
Our story starts at the very beginning of
the 18th century.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:21.159
To help you understand it better, we should
quickly present a few concepts about feudal

00:02:21.159 --> 00:02:22.159
Japan.

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:26.209
At that time, the country had an emperor,
but his role was mostly symbolic.

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:31.540
The true power was held by the shogun because
he had command over the military.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:36.680
In 1701, when the events took place, Japan
was almost halfway through the Tokugawa period,

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.909
also known as the Edo Period, because that
is where the shogunate established its seat

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:45.390
of power while the emperor was still based
in Kyoto.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:50.019
Edo is better known today as Tokyo.

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:54.760
Although Higashiyama was the Emperor of Japan
back then, the man actually in charge was

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.569
Tokugawa Tsunayoshi, the fifth shogun of the
Tokugawa dynasty.

00:02:59.569 --> 00:03:03.959
And the shogun exerted his power throughout
the land with the help of 300 feudal lords

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:05.769
called daimyo.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:10.999
One of those daimyo (and the one pertinent
to us today) was Asano Naganori, the third

00:03:10.999 --> 00:03:14.319
member of the Asano clan to rule over the
Akō Domain.

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:20.379
In 1701, he and another noble named Kamei
Korechika were tasked with organizing a reception

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:26.109
for some of the emperor’s ambassadors visiting
Edo Castle as part of their service known

00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:28.400
as sankin kōtai.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.200
Sankin kōtai was a policy developed by the
Tokugawa shoguns to help them keep an eye

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.030
on their feudal lords and to minimize their
resources so they didn’t get any funny ideas

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.189
about revolting.

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:43.029
Basically, it meant that the daimyo had to
split their time between their own domains

00:03:43.029 --> 00:03:44.209
and Edo Castle.

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:49.059
For several months at a time, every feudal
lord took his family and his retainers and

00:03:49.059 --> 00:03:52.260
went to live in Edo where he served the shogun
directly.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:58.099
His family (and, most importantly, his heir)
stayed in Edo whenever the daimyo left to

00:03:58.099 --> 00:04:03.430
look after his fiefdom and they were basically
hostages of the shogun to ensure that the

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.769
lord behaved himself.

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:09.311
Moreover, the Edo residence of the lord plus
all the tasks he had to perform for the shogun

00:04:09.311 --> 00:04:13.339
while he was there were all paid out of his
pocket which meant less money to raise an

00:04:13.339 --> 00:04:15.680
army that could be used against the shogun.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:20.030
Anyway, it was Asano Naganori’s time to
perform his sankin kōtai.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:25.140
In order for him and Kamei to organize a proper
reception for the imperial ambassadors, they

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:29.760
needed lessons in court etiquette and protocol
from one of the shogun’s high officials

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.780
- a man named Kira Yoshinaka who was a kōke,
meaning a master of ceremonies.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:39.500
Of course, for his services, Kira expected
gifts and monetary compensation.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.110
Kira and the two daimyo did not get along.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.490
We are not sure exactly what the reason was.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:49.199
Mitford said that the Edo official “was
a man greedy of money” who wasn’t happy

00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:50.620
with the “gifts” he received.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:54.810
Other sources said he was an arrogant man
who treated the two nobles with contempt and

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:55.810
ridicule.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:59.681
Either way, his actions and attitude became
too much to bear, but it was actually the

00:04:59.681 --> 00:05:04.210
other daimyo, Lord Kamei, who first decided
he wanted to kill Kira.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.979
He announced his intention to his retainers
during a meeting, saying that he had made

00:05:07.979 --> 00:05:12.830
up his mind and, the following day, he would
strike down Kira after the first insult and

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.900
then would suffer the consequences.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:19.710
His servants had no choice but to accept their
master’s decision, but his councillor looked

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.889
for another solution.

00:05:20.889 --> 00:05:25.449
He realized that the only way to get through
to the official was with a bribe so he collected

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:29.330
all the money he could and rode off that night
to Kira’s mansion.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.009
There, Kamei’s servant presented him with
a thousand ounces of silver, plus another

00:05:33.009 --> 00:05:34.310
hundred for his retainers.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.120
This bribe had a miraculous effect on Kira.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.889
The next day, he apologized to Kamei for his
conduct and, from then on, treated him with

00:05:41.889 --> 00:05:42.889
respect.

00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:44.810
His behavior towards Asano, however, remained
unchanged.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:50.599
If anything, it became even worse as Kira
was now angry that the lord from Ako didn’t

00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:52.970
follow his fellow nobleman’s example.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:57.860
For a long time, Asano Naganori took the insults
in silence, but he eventually reached his

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:58.860
limit.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.590
At one point, Kira pointed to his foot and
said that the ribbon of his sock had come

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.199
untied and told the lord to bend down and
tie it for him.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:10.469
Although burning with rage, Asano did this,
but afterwards Kira continued to mock him,

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:15.449
saying that he was a clumsy country boor who
did it improperly.

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:16.449
That was enough.

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:21.080
Asano took out a small sword called a wakizashi
and attacked the official, but only managed

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:25.009
a cut on Kira’s face before guards separated
them.

00:06:25.009 --> 00:06:28.780
Even though the injuries were minor, the consequences
were grave.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:33.500
Although he deserved it, Kira was still a
powerful official of the shogun, not to mention

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.090
that any kind of violence was forbidden at
Edo Castle.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:42.789
Asano Naganori was condemned to commit seppuku,
a ritual suicide by disembowelment.

00:06:42.789 --> 00:06:46.930
His death also meant the death of his clan
- his lands and goods were confiscated while

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:53.479
his retainers became ronin, meaning samurai
without masters.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:57.291
The Revenge Plot

00:06:57.291 --> 00:07:01.620
Revenge for Asano’s death had been expressly
forbidden by the shogun, but for some men

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:02.889
this mattered little.

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:08.130
The Ako daimyo had hundreds of retainers,
but 47 of the most loyal banded together with

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:11.840
the intent of seeking vengeance on behalf
of their former master.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:17.289
Led by Asano’s former principal councillor,
Ōishi Kuranosuke Yoshio, they became the

00:07:17.289 --> 00:07:18.419
47 ronin.

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:24.219
Now Kira may have been a corrupt, arrogant,
and reprehensible man, but he was no fool.

00:07:24.219 --> 00:07:28.610
He realized that, even with the shogun’s
decree, some of Asano’s former men might

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:30.550
feel duty-bound to seek revenge.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:36.410
Therefore, he surrounded himself at all times
by a host of guards provided by a daimyo named

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.069
Uyesugi Sama who was his father-in-law.

00:07:39.069 --> 00:07:42.840
The ronin could have attempted to take on
Kira and his men in open battle.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:47.219
They were all quite prepared to die for their
vengeance since they realized that, even if

00:07:47.219 --> 00:07:50.990
they were successful, they would, most likely,
be executed anyway.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:55.719
However, what they could not risk was Kira
getting away during the fight as they would

00:07:55.719 --> 00:07:59.419
almost certainly get only one shot at it.

00:07:59.419 --> 00:08:03.849
Therefore, they needed the Edo official to
get rid of his bodyguards and, for that, they

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:06.729
needed to convince him that there was no threat.

00:08:06.729 --> 00:08:11.139
To achieve their goal, the ronin all pretended
to get on with their lives and go their separate

00:08:11.139 --> 00:08:12.139
ways.

00:08:12.139 --> 00:08:15.550
Like many of the other retainers who once
worked for the Asano clan, they found new

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:21.219
professions - some became merchants, others
became carpenters, some even posed as monks.

00:08:21.219 --> 00:08:25.870
Out of them all, Ōishi went to the greatest
lengths to allay Kira’s suspicion.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.900
As Asano’s most trusted servant, he was
also the one the official feared the most

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.570
because it was expected of him to seek revenge.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:37.310
Instead, Ōishi relocated to Kyoto with his
family where he became a drunkard and a womanizer.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:41.490
He knew he had Kira’s spies on his tail,
watching everything he did and reporting back

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:46.580
to Edo so he had to dedicate himself completely
to this new role, regardless of the shame

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.690
it brought upon him.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:52.040
He would spend his days in bars and brothels,
stumbling drunk through the streets and causing

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:58.740
a scene so everyone would know what had become
of Ōishi, once proud samurai of the Ako daimyo.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:03.301
The most notorious incident happened with
a man from Satsuma who recognized Ōishi passed

00:09:03.301 --> 00:09:04.350
out in the street.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:09.760
Disgusted with him, he called him “fool
and craven” and “unworthy the name of

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:10.760
a samurai.”

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.170
He then kicked and spat on him.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:16.430
Ōishi accepted everything, but he then went
even further.

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:20.680
His wife, although she knew of her husband’s
plan, could no longer stand the shame.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:25.330
She begged him to show some restraint, but
this only served to spur him on even further.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:29.510
He concluded that a man in his position would
likely be abandoned by his family.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.370
Because his wife knew it was all an act, she
did not want to actually leave her husband,

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:37.090
so Ōishi left her and told her to take the
children, too.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:42.500
Only his eldest, Ōishi Chikara, stayed by
his side, as he was one of the 47 ronin.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.620
And so Ōishi carried on.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:49.040
Meanwhile, all his actions were reported back
to Kira and, eventually, his dedication paid

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.040
off.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.320
After over a year and a half later, the official
started to feel safe again, believing that

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:59.311
Asano’s former samurai had left their past
lives behind them, vengeance and all.

00:09:59.311 --> 00:10:03.300
He sent most of his guards back to their lord
and, once again, was only protected by his

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.630
own much smaller retinue.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:09.920
While Ōishi was giving his Oscar-worthy performance,
some of the other ronin did their part by

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.820
getting jobs in Edo in anticipation of the
attack.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.990
They observed the layout of Kira’s house,
looked for places to enter and exit, studied

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:20.260
his movements, and gathered information about
his retainers.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:25.440
They also started smuggling and stockpiling
weapons which they had to do in great secrecy.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.820
As we previously mentioned, not everyone could
just walk around Edo armed to the teeth, not

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:33.850
to mention that it would have surely raised
a few eyebrows if Asano’s former retainers,

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:38.380
who were now supposed to be craftsmen and
merchants, started equipping themselves like

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:39.380
samurai again.

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:44.021
Things were going pretty smoothly and, once
Kira sent his army away and Ōishi was no

00:10:44.021 --> 00:10:49.310
longer being spied on, it was all a matter
of waiting for the opportune time…

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:55.320
The Attack on Kira’s Mansion

00:10:55.320 --> 00:11:01.050
Almost two years had passed since the death
of Asano Naganori, but on December 14, 1702,

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:04.640
the 47 ronin were ready to avenge their former
master.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.850
It was a cold, snowy day and the wind howled
with fury.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:12.470
The ronin lurked patiently in the shadows,
waiting for midnight to launch their assault.

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:16.760
The night before, they held one final feast
together as the plan was to turn themselves

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.180
in and accept the death sentence that was
sure to come.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:23.300
Of course, this would be after they chopped
off Kira’s head and delivered it as an offering

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:24.610
to their master’s tomb.

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:26.930
The signal for the attack was the beating
of a drum.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:31.690
All the ronin also carried a shrill whistle
with them which they would blow if they found

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:32.830
and slain their target.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.760
The samurai had split into two groups.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:38.910
One was led by Ōishi and would charge through
the front gate while a smaller group led by

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:44.180
his son would cover the side entrance to ensure
that Kira would not slip through their grasp.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.320
They knew that there would be collateral damage.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:49.890
Killing Kira’s retainers was unavoidable
as they would surely try to protect their

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:50.890
master.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:55.450
However, Ōishi urged his brethren to avoid
hurting any women, children, old men, and

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:58.620
any other helpless persons they might run
into.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:02.690
On the night in question, the ronin leader
even sent one of his companions to Kira’s

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:06.330
neighbors to inform them of who they were
and what they intended to do.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:10.250
The messenger assured the neighbors that they
were neither thieves, nor ruffians, and that

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.290
no harm would come to them as long as they
did not try to interfere.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:17.620
Indeed, the neighbors found these terms perfectly
agreeable and none of them tried to come to

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:21.750
the official’s aid because none of them
liked Kira, in the first place.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.470
At least, that is how he is portrayed in every
retelling of this story.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.240
Some historians indicated that the master
of ceremonies may have been more popular in

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:31.760
real life in his hometown because he helped
develop farmland and build dikes.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:35.000
With that matter settled, it was finally time
to strike.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:39.540
Ōishi began beating his drum and the ronin
stormed the house of Kira Yoshinaka.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:43.950
Ten of the samurai climbed the rooftops, took
out their bows and kept a watch on the courtyard

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:46.710
to make sure nobody escaped to call for reinforcements.

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:50.920
Meanwhile, the frontal assault team led by
Ōishi broke into the main hall where it was

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.180
greeted by ten of Kira’s soldiers.

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:57.490
A fight ensued, but the ronin were more prepared
and determined compared to the retainers who

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:59.540
had just been disturbed from their slumber.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:03.740
Ōishi’s group managed to take down their
opponents without losing a single man.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:07.662
Meanwhile, Ōishi Chikara and the other ronin
made their way through the garden and were

00:13:07.662 --> 00:13:10.050
fighting other guards in the back of the house.

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:14.480
Eventually, the two groups reunited and headed
towards Kira’s private chambers together.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:19.830
As Ōishi predicted, some of Kira’s men
tried to make a getaway and bring word to

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:23.690
their master’s father-in-law, Uyesugi Sama,
who would have sent a small army to eradicate

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:24.690
the intruders.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:28.000
However, they were all struck down by the
archers prowling the rooftops.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:30.760
There would be no help for Kira on that day.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:35.290
The fight went on until there were only three
of Kira’s retainers left standing, but these

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.850
were his best samurai.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:42.480
They were Kobayashi Hehachi, Waku Handaiyu,
and Shimidzu Ikkaku.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:46.800
They were all that stood between the ronin
and Kira’s private room, but they proved

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.420
to be quite a lot to handle.

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:53.000
The three expert swordsmen defended their
point with fierce intensity and even managed

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.630
to drive the ronin back.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:58.470
Seeing that his men were tired and starting
to lose heart, Ōishi shouted at them with

00:13:58.470 --> 00:13:59.470
rage.

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:02.800
They had already forfeited their lives, so
why were they shrinking in their resolution

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.800
now?

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:08.310
They should go in there and either kill their
opponents or die trying as fulfilling their

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:11.390
master’s cause was the “noblest ambition
of a retainer.”

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:16.690
He then commanded his son, Chikara, to go
engage the three samurai in combat.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:22.060
The young man obeyed his father, picked up
a spear and locked weapons with Waku Handaiyu.

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:26.700
Their brawl was too intense to be contained
in just one room and, soon enough, the two

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.120
were fighting in the garden.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:31.490
All seemed lost for the younger Ōishi when
he tripped and fell in the pond.

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:36.690
As Waku was getting ready to deliver a killing
blow, Chikara drew his sword and cut his opponent’s

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.000
leg, causing him to fall.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.310
The ronin then managed to get up and kill
Handaiyu before he could retaliate.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.640
When he went inside, Chikara discovered that
the rest of the ronin finally dispatched the

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.120
other two swordsmen, as well.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:56.130
There was nobody left to protect Kira.

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:57.130
The Search for Kira

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.160
The ronin opened Kira’s private chambers,
but all they found was young Kira Sahioye,

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:00.160
the kōke’s son.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:04.080
He wielded a halberd and tried in vain to
defend his position, but he was too weak and

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:07.870
inexperienced to pose a real threat to one
ronin, let alone dozens of them.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:11.060
He attacked and was wounded, but the samurai
allowed him to flee.

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:15.730
There was only one target they had on their
collective minds so the search started for

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:17.030
Kira Yoshinaka.

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:20.970
The ronin split into several small parties
and completely ransacked the mansion, but

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:23.550
there was no trace of the imperial official.

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:27.570
All they could find were weeping women and
children who, in accordance with Ōishi’s

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.060
request, were left alone.

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:33.200
The ronin felt despondent and, at one point,
even contemplated committing suicide then

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.660
and there as they feared they had failed their
mission.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:40.540
However, while going through Kira’s bedroom,
Ōishi felt that his bed was still warm which

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.980
meant that he was sleeping in it when the
attack began.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:47.170
Kira had to be somewhere near, so they started
a new search.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.620
This time around, the samurai were more fortunate.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:53.170
One of them made the inspired choice to take
down a large picture which was hanging on

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:54.170
the wall.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:57.670
Behind it, they discovered a secret tunnel
which led outside to a small courtyard where

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:00.000
there was a storage room for firewood and
charcoal.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.200
At the other end of the tunnel, there were
two more guards lying in wait, but they were

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:07.200
no match and were quickly struck down by the
ronin.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:11.380
Inside the outhouse, the samurai found an
elderly man in his 60s, dressed as a noble.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:15.740
The man refused to give his name, but the
ronin were convinced they had found Kira Yoshinaka.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:19.870
Ōishi was able to confirm the identity of
the elderly stranger when he recognized the

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:25.190
scar that his master left him during his attack
that started this whole chain of events.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:29.540
Despite the ronin’s hatred for this man,
it was trumped by Ōishi’s sense of honor

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.260
and respect for the traditions of a samurai.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:37.010
He actually kneeled down and bowed his head
in deference to Kira, and informed him that

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:42.200
they were the former retainers of Asano Naganori,
there to seek justice for their master.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:46.230
He then gave the official the chance of a
nobleman’s death by committing seppuku.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:51.550
According to some versions, Ōishi even produced
the same wakizashi that his master used, but

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:55.070
this may be one of Mitford’s added elements
for dramatic effect.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:59.770
Either way, Kira had no interest in any kind
of death so he kept begging for mercy.

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:03.460
Unsurprisingly, given all they went through,
this had no effect on the ronin.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:07.289
Eventually tiring of the old man’s pleas,
Ōishi forced him on his knees and cut off

00:17:07.289 --> 00:17:11.200
his head.The ronin collected Kira’s head
in a bucket and prepared to leave, but made

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:16.839
sure to put out all of the lights so as not
to start a fire that might damage the neighbors’

00:17:16.839 --> 00:17:18.290
houses.

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:22.650
The Final Road

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:27.500
With their mission accomplished, the 47 ronin
embarked on a new journey to Sengaku-ji in

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:32.080
Takanawa where their master’s grave was
located with the intent of presenting Kira’s

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:36.020
head as an offering and fulfillment of their
duty before turning themselves in.

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:37.020
They had to hurry.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:40.680
Word of their deed had spread quickly throughout
the town and, when it reached Lord Uyesugi

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.640
Sama, he would have surely sent his men to
cut them down.

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:47.030
But they soon discovered that, apart from
him, everyone else was very impressed with

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:48.030
their actions.

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:50.990
It was, after all, what was expected of a
true samurai.

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:56.680
Word even reached a chief daimyo named Matsudaira
Aki, a former superior of the Asano clan,

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:01.010
who was greatly pleased with the ronin and
sent his own guards to ensure their protection

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.450
on the road to Takanawa.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:06.100
When the men reached the palace of the Prince
of Sendai, he, too, was satisfied with their

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:10.790
actions, and invited them to eat, drink and
rest, before continuing on their journey.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:16.600
And so the 47 ronin reached their destination
safely, performed the offering and said prayers

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:18.780
at their master’s tomb.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:22.110
Except that the 47 were actually 46.

00:18:22.110 --> 00:18:26.420
One of the ronin named Terasaka Kichiemon
had been absent from the procession to the

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:30.020
temple, although what exactly had happened
to him remains somewhat of a mystery.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:31.120
He didn’t die in the fight.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:35.250
He also didn’t commit seppuku alongside
the rest of the ronin as he lived to the ripe

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.620
old age of 83.

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:40.750
Mitford makes no mention of him in his version
of the events, although subsequent stories

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:45.640
suggest that Terasaka, because he was the
lowest in rank, was dispatched as a messenger

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:49.530
to travel to the Ako domain and tell Asano’s
family of what had happened.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:53.610
However, some historical documents indicate
that the ronin may have simply fled before

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:57.930
the attack and abandoned the raid altogether,
which is why he wasn’t sentenced to death

00:18:57.930 --> 00:18:59.150
like all the others.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:03.660
This goes against the triumphant, heroic tale
of the 47 ronin, though, and because there

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:08.190
is nothing conclusive to support it, this
part of the story usually gets “forgotten”

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:09.520
in retellings.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:14.920
As far as the other 46 ronin were concerned,
what they expected to happen, happened.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.150
They were arrested and sentenced to death.

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:21.680
However, because many saw their actions as
righteous and justified, they were not executed

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:24.040
as criminals, but were allowed to commit seppuku.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:28.660
Afterwards, they were all buried at Sengaku-ji
next to their lord.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:31.820
The 47th ronin joined them upon his death.

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:35.370
Their graves had become a popular place of
pilgrimage and one of the many people who

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:40.070
came to pay their respects was the same Satsuma
man who once kicked and spat on Ōishi in

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:44.860
the street when he thought the ronin had become
a drunkard unworthy of the name “samurai.”

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:49.550
He apologized for his insult and offered atonement
by taking out a dagger and stabbing himself

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:52.430
in the stomach, dying in front of Ōishi’s
grave.

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:53.720
This wasn’t a unique case.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:58.490
Mitford also mentions a samurai who, almost
170 years later, committed seppuku before

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:02.920
the grave of Ōishi Chikara because he was
refused entry into a clan.

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:07.340
In modern times, there is a festival at Sengaku
Temple every December 14.

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:11.890
Not as many cases of seppuku nowadays, but
people still turn up to help commemorate the

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:27.490
tale

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:37.370
of 
the 47 ronin.

